    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who commands an elite score of 76.13, making him our strongest play against Grayson Rodriguez. Despite a slight penalty for Rodriguez's potential to neutralize base stealers, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a must-start due to his massive raw projection and ideal batting order spot. Following closely is **Jonathan Aranda**, who earns a 67.64 score thanks to a favorable platoon edge against Troy Melton and a promotion to the #2 spot, which maximizes his efficiency. **Zack Gelof** also provides strong value at 60.79; while he takes a minor hit for facing an elite hold-focused pitcher, the combination of a high-park-factor environment and his prime #3 position makes him a cornerstone of the middle infield today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Luis Arraez**, who finished just outside the starting rotation with a score of 49.17. While his profile is stable, the optimizer favored the higher platoon-adjusted upside and power potential of **Gavin Sheets** and **Lawrence Butler** in their respective matchups. We remain wary of the heavy reliance on \"Lineup Pending\" statuses across the board, particularly with **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz**, as any late-scratch or order drop could significantly impact their utility. **Bryce Harper** carries some risk facing Bryan Woo, whose 3.59 xERA acts as an anchor on his projection, but his high xwOBA keeps him in the lineup despite the challenging matchup. Managers should monitor weather updates for all games, as any significant shifts could dampen the performance of **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Dylan Beavers**, both of whom are projected as marginal plays today.",
